==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Paris Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cyborg Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Consider Paris Cat an Area Attack version of [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]]. Spam meatshields to protect her from close-ranged pushers whilst stacking as many as possible to create a wall of quick and long ranged units. Can be really effective against enemies like [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and even [[R.Ost]] if three or more meatshields are in use.

Paris Cat's spammability allows for chipping damage, but high cost prevents her from being very effective for almost all enemies that outrange her (with 350 range or more). [[Master A.]] and [[Angelic Sleipnir]] are especially poor matchups because of their constant attacks, which can get Paris Cat continually knocked back before she lands even one hit. In these cases, you're advised to use units with even greater range.

Be careful when using Paris Cat with Cat CPU as her high cost and short recharge can drain your funds quickly.

==='''True Form'''===
Thanks to an attack buff and weaken immunity, Cyborg Cat has her cost effectiveness increased and becomes more useful against enemies that weaken, like [[Winged Pigge]]. The upgrade is relatively minor and unlikely to deserve priority over certain other True Forms, but still an important one nevertheless, as this unit needs the damage to be high in order to justify her cost and stay relevant as the game progresses.

Unless highly leveled, Cyborg Cat starts losing utility around late [[Stories of Legend]] to the early [[Uncanny Legends]] due to low health and enemy access to piercing attacks ([[Wave Attack|Waves]], Long Distance, Omni Strike and [[Surge Attack|Surges]]), making similar units like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama/Slapstick Cats]] the way to go, especially since the aforementioned two are more cost efficient. She still has a place, however, in 4-Crown difficulty due to her range advantage and lack of alternatives, especially against enemies like R.Ost and Winged Pigge that Cameraman can't even hit, though given other cost efficient midrangers such as Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]], [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], alongside Legend units such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Minka]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]], her value only lies in her accessibility compared to other options.

==='''Talents'''===
Cyborg Cat's first [[Talents|Talent]] gives her a chance (up to 50%) to [[Survive|survive]] lethal strikes, which greatly increases her cost-effectiveness by allowing her to stay on the field longer, a fantastic prospect for a unit as spammable as a meatshield and with a high cost, though unlike Cameraman's Survive talent this is not guaranteed, meaning that stacks can still run dangerously low. Her Defense and Attack Buff Talents will help her stay competitive stat-wise, though they will only be relevant if Cyborg Cat is also properly leveled. Toxic Immunity and Resist Freeze are situational, but they could allow her use against the likes of [[Gobble]] and [[Henry]]. Such enemies will still expose Cyborg to a quick demise if she's not accompanied by proper support units, and in the case of killing Gobble it's much faster to kill them with other cost efficient units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. Overall, these talents are good improvements, but better options exist which ultimately makes Cyborg less desirable to invest further into as you go further into the game, until the point of +levels.

==='''Orb'''===
An Effect Talent Orb's boost on a generalist such as Cyborg Cat would be negligible, so saving Effect Orbs for something else is recommended. She could, however, benefit from an Attack Up Orb for [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red Enemies]] or [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], as midrange attackers for these common traits are rare, though one can simply use Courier Cat and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] respectively as they provide more value for the cost, and Attack Up Orbs don't give much of an attack boost.

For Ability Talent Orbs, Cash Back will generally be best for reducing Cyborg's insane spam cost, but she still won't be viable in stages that don't give a lot of cash.

