==Trivia==
*Salon Cat, along with [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Actress Cat]] and [[Maiko Cat (Special Cat)|Geisha Cat]], is designed to "combine" with [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] and his variants to form a full body when they overlap.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Salon Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[The Divas (Removed Combo)|The Divas]] and [[Sexy Bathtime (Removed Combo)|Sexy Bathtime]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Salon Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Salon Cat
Has no limit when it comes to beauty care.
Works very well with Sexy Legs Cat.
Exceptional Range Attack (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Paris Cat
A very stylish cat that earned the name
Jeanne. Might be French, not sure.
Exceptional Range Attack (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Cyborg Cat
The ultimate bionic battle angel.
Perfect both aesthetically and technically.
Long distance Area Attack specialist.</pre>
*Paris Cat's appearance is most likely based on the heroine of the manga series ''[[wikipedia:The Rose of Versailles|The Rose of Versailles]]'', [[wikipedia:Oscar François de Jarjayes|Oscar François de Jarjayes]].
**More specifically, she may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Takarazuka Revue|Takarazuka Revue]], an all-female Japanese theatre troupe who have done numerous [[wikipedia:The Rose of Versailles musicals|musicals]] based on ''The Rose of Versailles''. Her nickname of "Jeanne" could be referring to how fans of the troupe often refer to its members as "Takarasienne" (タカラジェンヌ ''Takarajennu''), a portmanteau of ''Takarazuka'' and ''Parisienne''; this name is often abbreviated to just "Sienne" (ジェンヌ ''Jennu''), which is spelled and pronounced exactly like "Jeanne" in Japanese.
*Cyborg Cat's appearance is most likely based on Lady Armaroid, a cyborg from the manga series ''[[wikipedia:Cobra (manga)|Cobra]]''. They even share the same number of spikes on their shoulder pads.
*In the Spanish translation, Salon Cat and Paris Cat are referred to as "Gata" (feminine), while Cyborg Cat is referred to as "Gato" (masculine).
*Cyborg Cat is the only cat to have different True Form requirements in the Nintendo Switch and Mobile versions.

